# Copy to .dev.vars and fill in. .dev.vars is gitignored - never commit it.
#
# These are LOCAL secrets for `wrangler dev`. The deployed equivalents are set
# with `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>` and are NOT read from this file.
#
#   wrangler dev    -> reads .dev.vars
#   wrangler deploy -> reads secrets set via `wrangler secret put`

# One-time token that creates the very first admin. POST /api/admin/bootstrap
# succeeds only while the admins table is empty, and only when this matches.
# After the first admin exists the endpoint refuses regardless of the token, so
# leaking it later buys nothing.
#
# Generate one with:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN="replace-me-with-32-random-bytes"

# There is no password-pepper or KDF-iteration variable here by design. The
# password is never sent to the Worker: the panel derives a verifier with
# PBKDF2-SHA256 in the browser and the Worker stores its SHA-256. The iteration
# count lives in admins.iterations, per row, so raising it later does not need a
# redeploy. See "Admin authentication" in README.md for why.

# Personal access token for the GitHub repository that hosts Wafi X releases.
# Only needed from phase 3, when the panel starts creating GitHub Releases and
# uploading latest.json. Scope: `contents: write` on that one repository, and
# nothing else.
#
# Why GitHub and not the Worker: src-tauri/src/update_identity.rs pins both the
# artifact filename prefix and the download host to a github.com release URL, so
# the updater feed cannot move without a deliberate change to that file. The
# panel publishes to GitHub and records the result in wafx_releases.
# GITHUB_PAT="github_pat_..."

# Uncomment only to test against a real GitHub repo from `wrangler dev`.
# Without it, publishing is a no-op that returns the payload it would have sent,
# which is what you want locally: no accidental release from a dev machine.
# GITHUB_REPO="owner/repo"

# Where the admin panel is reached from. Must match [vars] PUBLIC_ORIGIN in
# wrangler.toml. Kept here as well so a dev session can point somewhere else
# (a tunnel, another worker) without editing the committed config.
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN="http://localhost:8787"
